From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:09:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: mark PCI 0x110e as a TME firmware image

Stock peach amss20.bin is two ELF files. Tell MHI, so BHIe sends
only the second one. The same firmware asks for memory region
0xb. Allocate it the way upstream ath12k does for the LPASS
shared region. That allocation has not been retested: reloading
the module on the same boot oopsed in qrtr before QMI came back.

Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.7 <noreply@x.ai>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
index ee87f00bc..3b29052fc 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
@@ -256,6 +256,12 @@ int ath12k_mhi_register(struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci)
 	mhi_ctrl->sbl_size = SZ_512K;
 	mhi_ctrl->seg_len = SZ_512K;
 	mhi_ctrl->fbc_download = true;
+	/*
+	 * PCI 0x110e (peach) firmware is two ELF files. The second one
+	 * starts at sbl_size, and that is what BHIe has to send.
+	 */
+	if (ab_pci->pdev->device == 0x110e)
+		mhi_ctrl->tme_supported_image = true;
 	mhi_ctrl->runtime_get = ath12k_mhi_op_runtime_get;
 	mhi_ctrl->runtime_put = ath12k_mhi_op_runtime_put;
 	mhi_ctrl->status_cb = ath12k_mhi_op_status_cb;
